# The test playground's content (#321.2): a goblin that stands peacefully until a lever makes it fight, a second
# lever that respawns it, every weapon and the consumables lying in the room, and a hero at the game's maximum
# level who knows every rune. The levers are driven through the test channel: `playground pull mode` /
# `playground pull respawn` give the lever script exactly what a hand pull gives it (#38); `playground kill` kills
# the NPC as a hit would. status.json: playground.{npc, npcMode, npcAlive, npcLife, npcLifeMax, npcAtSpot, items},
# player.level, player.allRunes (src/core/CommandChannel.cpp).
#   .\scripts\dev\smoke-test.ps1 -Playground -VrSim idle -Sequence playground-levers
# (@playground below makes xrs-run.ps1 start the generated level; area 30.)
@sim idle
@playground

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false
@assert area eq 30

# The content is there. Level 10 is the cap: ARX_PLAYER_Modify_XP only levels up while i < 11 (src/game/Player.cpp),
# so 10 is the highest level the game's own XP table (178000 xp) reaches. Items: a lower bound, the game data cannot
# be listed here - the weapon classes (dagger, sword, two-handed sword, axe, mace/club, bow = 6 at least) plus a
# potion, a food and a scroll make 9 at least; 10 leaves room for a second kind without letting a missing group pass.
@assert player.level eq 10
@assert player.allRunes eq true
@assert playground.npcAlive eq true
@assert playground.npcMode eq peaceful
@assert playground.npcAtSpot eq true
@assert playground.npcLifeMax gt 0
@assert playground.items ge 10
@remember life0 player.life
@remember lifemax playground.npcLifeMax

# 1. Peaceful: the hero stands a step from the NPC (layout.mjs: NPC_SPOT x 200, z 100 from the room centre 8000/8000;
# setpos takes the EYE: floor y 0 - 170 = -170; yaw 0 faces north) and nothing happens for 10 s
setpos 8200 -170 8000 0
@frames 30
@wait 10000
@assert player.life eq {life0}
@assert playground.npcMode eq peaceful
@assert playground.npcAlive eq true

# 2. The mode lever: aggressive, the NPC attacks and the hero loses life within 20 s
playground pull mode
@frames 5
@assert playground.npcMode eq aggressive
@until player.life lt {life0} 20s

# 3. Pulled again: peaceful
playground pull mode
@frames 5
@assert playground.npcMode eq peaceful

# 4. Dead, then the respawn lever: alive at its spot with full life, the mode as it was
playground kill
@until playground.npcAlive eq false 5s
playground pull respawn
@until playground.npcAlive eq true 5s
@frames 5
@assert playground.npcLife eq {lifemax}
@assert playground.npcAtSpot eq true
@assert playground.npcMode eq peaceful
@assert errors eq 0
